+//   y = d_f, the focus distance in metres.
+//   z = the circle of confusion cap in gather units (r_DepthOfFieldLensModelMaxCoC), NEGATED
+//       when r_DepthOfFieldLensModelDebug is on - a cap is a positive quantity by construction,
+//       so its sign is a free flag and costs no lane in a constant that has none to spare.
+// The SPLAT and the GHOST draws never form a circle of confusion themselves (they read the
+// gather's own CoC texture), so for those two passes x and y are unused and z carries the
+// SPLAT's own cap in native pixels instead.
+//   w = k_sa, spherical aberration. The one lane every consumer reads the same way.
+float4 vDofLensModel;
+
+// Thin lens, signed, in the gather's existing CoC units. This is the whole point of the round:
+// a real lens has no "focus range" and no quadratic ramp - the blur is fixed by focal length,
+// f-number, focus distance and sensor size, and the near/far split falls out of the SIGN of the
+// defocus rather than out of two independently authored ramps.
+//
+// The lens flaws fold in exactly where they do on the stock path, because they are the same
+// physical statements: field curvature bends the object distance BEFORE the lens sees it, edge
+// softness is a residual far-side blur floor after it, and the minimum-Z near blur is a camera
+// BODY effect that must not be bent by the curved focal surface.
+void LensModelCoC(in float4 depths, in float fFieldR2, out float4 nearCoC, out float4 farCoC)
+{
